course: dictionary
lesson: 11432
title: Actively
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Actively is an adverb, so it tells you how someone does something. It comes from the word active, which means busy or lively. When you see actively, ask: is someone taking part, or just watching?
explain: «Mia listens actively in every lesson, asking questions and joining in.» Mia is not just sitting and hearing the words. She is busy with her ears, her mind and her voice, so actively means in a lively, taking-part way.
explain: Actively can also mean really and on purpose. «The rescue team was actively looking for help.» They were not waiting for help to come. They were trying hard to find it.
explain: Use the clues around the word. If someone is moving, joining in or doing something on purpose, actively fits. If someone is sitting back and waiting, it does not.
fact: Actively means in a busy, lively way, by doing things rather than just watching or waiting.
fact: Actively can also mean really and on purpose, as in «actively looking for help».
fact: Actively is an adverb, so it describes how someone does an action.
fact: In school, to listen actively means to look at the speaker, think about what is said, and join in.
fact: Playing or moving actively, such as running and jumping, helps keep your body fit.
exercise: «Ravi listens actively, looking at the speaker and asking questions.» What does actively mean here? | *In a busy, lively way, taking part | Angrily | Quietly, while half asleep | Only sometimes, when he feels like it
exercise: «The children were actively helping to clean the park.» What does actively mean? | Reluctantly, with a frown | Sitting and watching | *Really doing it, on purpose
exercise: In PE, Lena runs and jumps actively for the whole hour. What does actively tell us? | She is sleeping in the corner | She is sitting down to rest | *She is moving and taking part, not just watching | She is late for the lesson
test: «The rescue team was actively searching for the lost dog.» What does actively mean? | *On purpose, really looking | Sleepily, with her eyes closed | Only on Sundays | Happily, without a care
test: Which word is the opposite of actively, when someone just sits and watches? | *Passively | Loudly | Quickly | Helpfully
exam: «Maya was actively involved in the school project, and her ideas helped everyone.» What does actively mean in this sentence? | Feeling sleepy | *Taking a real part, doing things | Eating a lot | Being quietly unseen
